{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "בהעלותך", :translit "b'ha'alotkha", :gloss "when you kindle"} {:he "סמך נרות לחנוכה", :translit "samakh nerot le-chanukah", :gloss "the lamps adjoin to Hanukkah"} {:he "לפרסומי ניסא בנרות", :translit "le-farsumei nisa be-nerot", :gloss "for publicizing the miracle through lamps"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Parsha of the lamps read as an allusion to the future miracle of Hanukkah lamps"}], :frame {:text "The institution of Hanukkah lamps publicizing a miracle is discussed in tractate Shabbat 21b, where the sages debate how many lamps are lit to publicize the miracle (pirsumei nisa). The linking of the menorah's lamps to the Hanukkah lamps is an established midrashic move found in sources such as Pesikta Rabbati 2.", :sources ["Shabbat 21b" "Pesikta Rabbati 2"]}} {:quotes [{:he "בהעלתך את", :translit "b'ha'alatkha et", :gloss "when you kindle [object marker]"} {:he "עשה בה מעלות", :translit "aseh ba ma'alot", :gloss "make in it stages"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :gematria, :a "בהעלתך את", :b "עשה בה מעלות"}], :frame nil} {:quotes [{:he "אל מול פני המנורה יאירו", :translit "el mul p'nei ha-menorah ya'iru", :gloss "toward the face of the menorah they shall shine"} {:he "כי אני איני צריך לאורה", :translit "ki ani eino tzarikh le-orah", :gloss "for I do not need its light"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "The verse's directive to face the lamps toward the menorah is explained: the light is not for God"}], :frame {:text "The midrash asks why the lamps must face the menorah's central stem, and answers that it testifies that God does not need the light, as stated in Proverbs 6:23 — the commandment is a lamp and the Torah is light. This idea appears in Bamidbar Rabbah 15:7 and is cited by Rashi on Numbers 8:2.", :sources ["Bamidbar Rabbah 15:7" "Rashi on Numbers 8:2" "Proverbs 6:23"]}} {:quotes [{:he "פני המנורה יאירו", :translit "p'nei ha-menorah ya'iru", :gloss "face of the menorah they shall shine"} {:he "וכי אני לאורך צריך", :translit "ukhi ani le-orekha tzarikh", :gloss "do I need your light"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :gematria, :a "פני המנורה יאירו", :b "וכי אני לאורך צריך"}], :frame nil} {:quotes [{:he "שבעת הנרות", :translit "shiv'at ha-nerot", :gloss "the seven lamps"} {:he "חנכ\"ל שצ\"ם", :translit "chak\"l shatz\"m", :gloss "[abbreviations for the seven planets]"} {:he "בהעלותך את הנרות", :translit "b'ha'alotkha et ha-nerot", :gloss "when you kindle the lamps"} {:he "להעלות נר תמיד", :translit "le-ha'alot ner tamid", :gloss "to kindle a lamp continually"} {:he "נר ואח\"כ נרות", :translit "ner ve-achar kach nerot", :gloss "lamp and afterward lamps"} {:he "נרות ואח\"כ נר", :translit "nerot ve-achar kach ner", :gloss "lamps and afterward lamp"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Seven lamps correspond to the seven planets named by the abbreviations חנכ\"ל שצ\"ם"} {:kind :other, :note "Word-order linkage between two verses to derive Beit Hillel and Beit Shammai practices"}], :frame {:text "The correspondance of the seven lamps to the seven classical planets appears in Bamidbar Rabbah 15:7. The debate between Beit Shammai and Beit Hillel regarding the order of lighting Hanukkah lamps — Beit Shammai decreasing from eight to one, Beit Hillel increasing from one to eight — is recorded in Shabbat 21b. Beit Hillel's principle of increasing in holiness and not decreasing is stated in Shabbat 21b.", :sources ["Bamidbar Rabbah 15:7" "Shabbat 21b"]}} {:quotes [{:he "להעל", :translit "le-ha'al", :gloss "to kindle"} {:he "ות נר תמיד", :translit "vot ner tamid", :gloss "[continuation forming] a lamp continually"} {:he "ס\"ת", :translit "sat", :gloss "[final letters abbreviation]"} {:he "תרד", :translit "tered", :gloss "you shall go down"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :sofei-tevot, :phrase "ות נר תמיד", :spells "תרד"}], :frame nil}], :arithmetic [{:kind :other, :note "Parsha of the lamps read as an allusion to the future miracle of Hanukkah lamps", :by :selah, :ran? false} {:kind :gematr